## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heightfield_xform.html
- Summary (EN): Applies a 3D transform (translate, rotate, scale, shear) to a height layer, with optional separate scale and offset of the height values.
- Résumé (FR) : Applique une transformation 3D (translation, rotation, échelle, cisaillement) à une couche de hauteur, avec mise à l'échelle et décalage propres des valeurs de hauteur.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: the height layer to transform"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Transform Order / Rotate Order", "meaning": "sequence of transform and rotation operations"}, {"name": "Translate, Rotate, Scale, Shear, Uniform Scale", "meaning": "XYZ movement, rotation in degrees, non-uniform and overall scaling, shear"}, {"name": "Invert Transformation", "meaning": "applies the inverse, which undoes a matching transform"}, {"name": "Pivot Translate / Pivot Rotate", "meaning": "moves and rotates the local pivot used for transforms"}, {"name": "Apply Transform Scale to Height", "meaning": "scales height pixels with the 3D transform"}, {"name": "Grid Scale", "meaning": "stretches or contracts the layer horizontally"}, {"name": "Height Scale", "meaning": "stretches or contracts the height values vertically"}, {"name": "Height Offset", "meaning": "shifts the height values up or down"}]

- Caveats: ["Height-specific scaling is separate from the 3D transform unless Apply Transform Scale to Height is enabled."]

